  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. `channel` is on the `OrderPlaced` event (`src/core/events.ts:16`, populated at `:50`), and I can't remove it from there safely.\n\n**Why I stopped:** ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repositories, consume `OrderPlaced`. Changes to the event have to be additive, and removals have to go through deprecation. Nothing in this repo reads `channel` from the event, but that tells us nothing about those two consumers. Dropping the field outright could break either of them in production. The same applies to `channel` in the `POST /orders` request and the order model, since `GET /orders/{id}` (ARCH-8) returns the order to web-storefront, and the response must stay backward compatible.\n\n**What I'd suggest instead:**\n1. Confirm with the billing-service and analytics-ingest owners that neither reads `channel`.\n2. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` on the event. Keep populating it, and make it optional in the request so callers can stop sending it.\n3. Remove it from the event and the order model once the consumers have been confirmed or updated and the deprecation window has passed.\n\n**Safe to do now if you want it:** I could do step 2. That would mean the deprecation notes, making `channel` optional on input with a fixed default in the event, and updating the validation and tests to match. I could also do the full removal if you can confirm the consumers don't use the field. Which would you like?",
